    "case_id": "mxh014",
    "case_summary": "A 65-year-old man presents with four months of low-grade fever and malaise. He also says he has lost 9 kg (20 lb) during this period and suffers from extreme fatigue. Past medical history is significant for a mitral valve replacement five years ago. His temperature is 38.1°C (100.6°F), respirations are 22/min, pulse is 102/min, and blood pressure is 138/78 mm Hg. On physical examination, there is a new onset 2/6 holosystolic murmur, loudest in the apical area of the precordium. Which of the following organisms is the most likely cause of this patient’s condition?\n\nOptions:\nA. *Pseudomonas aeruginosa*\nB. *Bartonella henselae*\nC. HACEK group organisms\nD. *Candida albicans*\nE. Beta-hemolytic streptococci\nF. *Staphylococcus aureus*\nG. Coagulase-negative *Staphylococcus spp.*\nH. *Pseudomonas* aeruginosa\nI. *Streptococcus bovis*\nJ. *Enterococcus*\n",
